    "summary": "Jazzy ’73 show with expansive Weather Report Suite and strong second set",
    "blurb": "The night glows on an experimental Weather Report Suite that lets the horn guests stretch out, while Loser pops as a first‑set highlight. The second set is brilliant, featuring a soaring He’s Gone and tight band interplay throughout.",
    "review": "September 26, 1973 at Buffalo’s War Memorial Auditorium captures the Grateful Dead in a wonderfully jazzy mood. A loose‑feeling soundboard still manages to convey the horn‑enhanced improvisations that lift the Weather Report Suite (Prelude*, Part 1, Let It Grow) into an expansive centerpiece, and Jerry’s guitar weaves through it with his characteristic lyrical phrasing. The first set offers solid moments—Here Comes Sunshine opens the show bright, Loser delivers a punchy, almost rock‑blues surge, and China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider rolls smoothly into the groove. The second set truly shines: He’s Gone unfolds with that 1973 melancholy intensity, Truckin’ and Eyes of the World roll seamlessly into the suite, and Sugar Magnolia closes the night on a high‑energy note. Across all recordings the band feels locked in, the horns add color without overwhelming the core sound, and the performance stands out as a vivid snapshot of the Dead’s early‑‘70s exploratory period.\n\nFor listeners seeking the clearest window into this night, the Miller‑patched soundboard (gd1973-09-26.sbd-repatched.miller.80198.sbeok.flac16) offers an excellent, clean mix with no dropouts, making it the most reliable source for both the nuanced first‑set moments and the soaring second‑set energy.",
